# CONTROL for `todo/t1310` — the `Box.new(...)` spelling of
# `sh_box_ctor_spelling_double_free.gg`, which is CORRECT on the self-host lane
# (emit rc 0, cc rc 0, run rc 0, correct output).
#
# It is committed because a defect whose discriminator is a SPELLING needs both
# spellings in the tree: without this file, `t1310`'s claim is a sentence, and
# the next reader has to reconstruct the control before they can believe it.
# Its test is LIVE — if this one ever starts failing too, the discriminator has
# moved and `t1310` is describing something else.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Box[String] b = Box.new(mk("xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx", "yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy"))
    print((*b))
